# Remaining scans on document access history

This update adds `RemainingScansByRule` to every DocumentAccessAudit returned
by your existing endpoint. It provides one balance per currently enabled rule
on the document's currently assigned policy. No new tables or columns are needed.

## Meaning of the balance

The balance is calculated immediately AFTER the recorded attempt, using that
entry's CreatedDate and Id. It is not the balance available now.

The existing audit table does not store the policy and rule settings used at
the time of each attempt. Consequently this implementation explicitly returns:

```json
"quotaCalculationBasis": "CurrentPolicyRules"
```

Historical balances are reconstructed from recorded quota-consuming attempts
against the CURRENT rule names, windows, maxima, enabled flags, and document
policy assignment. Changing those settings can change the balances shown for
older entries. These must not be presented as immutable original-rule snapshots.
To preserve actual historical balances and settings, capture them at access time
in the validation procedure; those facts cannot be recovered reliably for old
rows merely by changing this getter.

